  Answer #4
  
    Miss Bo-Peep must have had at least eight sheep in her flock. Eight posts
    arranged in a square would contain the same area as ten posts of an 
    oblong - of course, assuming that the posts were in both cases set in a 
    uniform distance apart.
    
